ngths range from 2√(225 - 81) = 24 to 30. Lengths 24 and 30 each occur once; each integer length 25 through 29 occurs twice. Thus there are 2 + 2 × 5 = 12 chords.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_125"],"coverage":"partial","flags":[],"questionId":"1991_AMC_12_Q10","reviewStatus":"machine_examined","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_250","cnm_065","cnm_125","cnm_074"],"id":"chord-distance-and-positions","label":"Count chords by their distance from the center","methodDirectNodeIds":{"chord-distance-and-positions":["cnm_h180","cnm_251","cnm_174","cnm_132","cnm_h020","cnm_h232"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_h180","cnm_251","cnm_174","cnm_132","cnm_h020","cnm_h232","cnm_250","cnm_065","cnm_125","cnm_074"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":11,"alignmentIds":["alignment:d80f5241f43281e1c465d17d"],"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"B, DF need not bisect ∠CDA","reason":"Write ∠A=α. The diameter gives ∠CDA=90°. Tangent geometry yields FC=FD=FA, ∠FDA=α, ∠CFD=2α, and ∠BCD=α. Thus F is the midpoint of CA and the other stated relations hold, but DF bisects ∠CDA only when α=45°.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_125"],"coverage":"partial","flags":[],"questionId":"1965_AMC_12_Q30","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_055","cnm_058","cnm_116","cnm_250","cnm_260"],"id":"right-triangle-congruence-and-angles","label":"Compare two right triangles","methodDirectNodeIds":{"right-triangle-congruence-and-angles":["cnm_254","cnm_262","cnm_125","cnm_121","cnm_137","cnm_138","cnm_117"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_254","cnm_262","cnm_125","cnm_121","cnm_137","cnm_138","cnm_117","cnm_055","cnm_058","cnm_116","cnm_250","cnm_260"]}]}],"canonicalNodeIds":["cnm_125"],"label":"全等判定：斜边、直角边（HL）","layer":"CN","meaning":"Practice covers aligned canonical concepts, with no claim of complete standard coverage or mastery.","nextOffset":null,"sourceNode":{"criteria":["能叙述 HL","能判断何时只能用 HL"],"description":"斜边和一条直角边分别相等的两个